{"code":"47-2031.00","title":"Carpenters","description":"Construct, erect, install, or repair structures and fixtures made of wood and comparable materials, such as concrete forms; building frameworks, including partitions, joists, studding, and rafters; and wood stairways, window and door frames, and hardwood floors. May also install cabinets, siding, drywall, and batt or roll insulation. Includes brattice builders who build doors or brattices (ventilation walls or partitions) in underground passageways.","jobZone":2,"kinds":{"R":{"score":6.75,"share":0.4796},"I":{"score":1.91,"share":0.0759},"A":{"score":2.18,"share":0.0984},"S":{"score":1.9,"share":0.0751},"E":{"score":1.79,"share":0.0659},"C":{"score":3.46,"share":0.2052}},"highPoints":["R","C"],"tasks":[{"id":23432,"text":"Measure and mark cutting lines on materials, using a ruler, pencil, chalk, and marking gauge.","core":true,"importance":4.05,"relevance":100,"frequency":5.42},{"id":23430,"text":"Follow established safety rules and regulations and maintain a safe and clean environment.","core":true,"importance":3.91,"relevance":100,"frequency":4.58},{"id":23433,"text":"Shape or cut materials to specified measurements, using hand tools, machines, or power saws.","core":true,"importance":3.83,"relevance":100,"frequency":4.55},{"id":23436,"text":"Select and order lumber or other required materials.","core":true,"importance":3.82,"relevance":100,"frequency":3.65},{"id":23434,"text":"Install structures or fixtures, such as windows, frames, floorings, trim, or hardware, using carpenters' hand or power tools.","core":true,"importance":3.77,"relevance":100,"frequency":4.35},{"id":23435,"text":"Verify trueness of structure, using plumb bob and level.","core":true,"importance":3.73,"relevance":100,"frequency":3.26},{"id":23437,"text":"Arrange for subcontractors to deal with special areas, such as heating or electrical wiring work.","core":true,"importance":3.65,"relevance":84.94,"frequency":3.51},{"id":23439,"text":"Build or repair cabinets, doors, frameworks, floors, or other wooden fixtures used in buildings, using woodworking machines, carpenter's hand tools, or power tools.","core":true,"importance":3.63,"relevance":100,"frequency":4.14},{"id":23446,"text":"Remove damaged or defective parts or sections of structures and repair or replace, using hand tools.","core":true,"importance":3.57,"relevance":100,"frequency":4.08},{"id":23440,"text":"Erect scaffolding or ladders for assembling structures above ground level.","core":true,"importance":3.56,"relevance":98.47,"frequency":2.67},{"id":23447,"text":"Install rough door and window frames, subflooring, fixtures, or temporary supports in structures undergoing construction or repair.","core":true,"importance":3.56,"relevance":95.87,"frequency":3.14},{"id":23445,"text":"Maintain job records and schedule work crew.","core":true,"importance":3.54,"relevance":80.87,"frequency":4.79},{"id":23449,"text":"Examine structural timbers and supports to detect decay, and replace timbers as required, using hand tools, nuts, and bolts.","core":true,"importance":3.52,"relevance":80.44,"frequency":2.37},{"id":23452,"text":"Fill cracks or other defects in plaster or plasterboard and sand patch, using patching plaster, trowel, and sanding tool.","core":true,"importance":3.5,"relevance":91.16,"frequency":3.73},{"id":23458,"text":"Dig or direct digging of post holes and set poles to support structures.","core":true,"importance":3.5,"relevance":80.86,"frequency":2.38},{"id":23448,"text":"Finish surfaces of woodwork or wallboard in houses or buildings, using paint, hand tools, or paneling.","core":true,"importance":3.47,"relevance":100,"frequency":3.38},{"id":23451,"text":"Cover subfloors with building paper to keep out moisture and lay hardwood, parquet, or wood-strip-block floors by nailing floors to subfloor or cementing them to mastic or asphalt base.","core":true,"importance":3.44,"relevance":82.07,"frequency":2.66},{"id":23442,"text":"Inspect ceili